      "title": "Robust legged robot state estimation using factor graph optimization",
      "takeaway": "This method paper addresses legged robot state estimation when foot contact classification fails, for example on slippery terrain, and when position drift grows during dynamic motions such as trotting. It presents a factor graph optimization method that tightly fuses and smooths inertial navigation, leg odometry, and visual odometry, reducing reliance on contact classification. The approach was demonstrated on the ANYmal quadruped navigating a realistic outdoor industrial environment with trotting, walking, obstacle crossing, and staircase ascent, decreasing relative position error by up to 55% and absolute position error by 76% compared to kinematic-inertial odometry. While reading, inspect how the factor graph handles contact uncertainty and visual degradation, and how the reported errors are defined.",
